userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Multiplying a vector by a scalar k stretches or shrinks its length by |k| while keeping the same line of action, and reverses its direction when k is negative.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A scalar multiple kv never leaves the line through v — |k| tells you how far along that line you go, and the sign of k tells you which of the two directions you go.
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "Multiplying a vector by a scalar k stretches or shrinks its length by |k| while keeping the same line of action, and reverses its direction when k is negative.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Four parallel arrows at an identical shallow upward slope (~17° above horizontal), stacked top to bottom and spread across nearly the full canvas width and height so length differences read clearly",
    "Dark navy arrow, longest, spanning most of the canvas width, labeled '3v' in italic just past its arrowhead (top row)",
    "Orange arrow labeled 'v' past its arrowhead, about one third the navy length (second row)",
    "Teal arrow labeled with a true stacked fraction — '1' over '2' with a horizontal fraction bar, followed by italic 'v' — half the length of v (third row)",
    "Red arrow pointing down-and-to-the-left, same length as v, labeled '−v' in italic beside its tail dot (bottom row)",
    "Small filled black dot at the tail (application point) of each arrow: left end for 3v, v and ½v; right end for −v",
    "Solid triangular arrowheads on every vector; uniform moderate line weight; generously sized italic labels for inline legibility",
    "Overlay-only: purple interactive arrow k·v drawn from the SAME tail dot as the orange v, on top of it (hidden by default)",
    "Overlay-only: faint gray dashed line of action extended through the orange v's tail in both directions (hidden by default)",
    "Overlay-only: small purple tick marks / ghost outlines on the dashed line at k = −1, 0, ½, 1, 3 to anchor the source multiples",
    "Common-tail-only: navy 3v, orange v, teal ½v and red −v all redrawn from one shared black dot, overlapping along the dashed line of action",
    "Side UI panel (outside the drawing canvas): color legend (navy 3v, orange v, teal ½v, red −v, purple k·v), and a live readout of k, resulting length |k|·|v| in units of |v|, and direction text ('same as v' / 'opposite to v' / 'zero vector')"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
